sentences.text:
Let the petitioners be released on bail on furnishing bail bond of Rs. 10,000/- (Ten thousand) each with two sureties Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.10770 of 2024(5) dt.12-07-2024 of like amount each to the satisfaction of learned Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate-1st, Patna, in connection Kanhaiya Prasad @ Kanhaya Prasad vs The State Of Bihar on 12 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/189697533/
2 with Economic Offence P.S. Case No. 13 of 2023 subject to the following conditions:
(i) one of the bailor should be the family member of the petitioners who shall provide official document to show his/her bona fide;
(ii) the petitioners shall appear on each and every date before the Trial Court and failure to do so for two consecutive dates without plausible reason will entail cancellation of their bail bond by the Trial Court itself;
(iii) the petitioners shall appear before the concerned police station every for next one year to mark their attendance;
(iii) the petitioners shall in no way try to induce or promise or threat the witnesses or tamper with the evidences, failing which the State shall be at liberty to take steps for cancellation of the bail bonds;
(iv) the petitioners shall desist from committing any criminal offence again, failing which the State shall be at liberty to take steps for cancellation of their bail bonds.
